    "created_at": "2026-04-22T15:16:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-04-22T15:16:28Z",
    "body": "Old issue I know, but:\nDuring my work I stumble a lot over these issues. I am developing custom web components, which can have custom components again in their slot and so on. Implementing a keyboard navigation compliant to for example a menubar or a simple dropdown to the likes of a WAI pattern is tedious. Maybe I am missing something but the need of basically parsing the DOM myself feels ugly and useless since simply pressing Tab seems to know exactly what the next element to focus is.\nFurthermore sth like a shadow DOM makes `document.activeElement` completely useless. Maybe the opinion is that everyone should implement this themselves, but I feel like there is a huge use-case for this and the current focus system seems more robust and capable than what most would implement.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
